    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, replacing the three separate checks.\n\n**Duplicate logic** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`):\n- Removed `rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, and `rejectDuplicateHousehold`.\n- Added `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner, normalizedTelephone)`, which builds the new owner's whole `identityKey` and rejects with 409 only when it exactly equals an existing owner's key. Existing owners' telephones are E.164-normalized and emails lower-cased before building their key, preserving the old normalization robustness.\n- Reordered `addOwner` so the household id is assigned first (when `sharesHousehold` is true), then the single identity check runs. Because telephone is part of the key, two same-household members with different telephones now get different keys and are **both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate, as the spec requires.\n\n**Response** (`identityKey` is returned):\n- Added a read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it).\n- Added `OwnerMapper.identityKey(owner)` deriving it from the stored (already-normalized) telephone, email, and household id, wired via a `@Mapping` expression like the other derived fields.\n\n**Exceptions**:\n- Added `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (\u2192 409) plus its handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (with `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`).\n- Deleted the now-unused `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`, `DuplicateOwnerEmailException`, `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` and their handlers/imports.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (two owners sharing a telephone \u2192 409) passes.",
